      <pubDate>Wed, 01 Mar 2023 09:00:45 -0600</pubDate>
      <title>Olentangy Trail Update — Crossing Safety Enhancements Unveiled</title>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">55244074</guid>
      <link>https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/OHCCC/bulletins/34af52a</link>
      <description>
        <![CDATA[<table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" align="center" class="gd_tbl_wrap"><tr><td style="background-color: #DCDCDC; margin: 0; padding: 0; width: 100% !important" bgcolor="#DCDCDC"><table class="main-table" width="600" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" id="yahoo" style="width: 600px; border-collapse: collapse;">

<tr>
<td style="padding: 15px 0 20px;" class="mobile-padding">
<table class="main-table" width="100%" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" style="background-color: #FFF; border-collapse: collapse;">

<tr>
<td id="header-bg" data-govdstyle="all" data-govdtitle="Header Background" style="border-left-style: none; border-right-style: none; border-top-style: none;">
<table class="main-table" width="100%" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse: collapse;">
<tr>
<td id="main-header" width="100%" data-govdstyle="all" data-govdtitle="Main Header" align="center" style="padding: 0px;">
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000; font-size: 12px; margin: 0 0 10px;">Having trouble viewing this email? <a href="https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/OHCCC/bulletins/34af52a">View it as a Web page</a>.</p>
<table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="border-collapse: collapse;"><tr><td align="center"><img class="govd_template_image" src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/OHCCC/2022/10/6562165/4368249/olentangy-trail-email-header_crop.png" style="width: 600px; height: auto !important; max-height: auto !important; border: none;" alt="Olentangy Trail" width="600" height="225"></td></tr></table>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>
<table class="main-table" width="100%" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse: collapse;">
<tr>
<td id="main-body" width="100%" data-govdstyle="all" data-govdtitle="Main Body" style="padding: 20px;">
<h1 style="line-height: 1.1; font-weight: bold; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 26px; text-align: left; color: #000000; margin: 0 0 10px;" align="left"><strong>Olentangy Trail Completion Update - Crossing Safety Enhancements Unveiled</strong></h1>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 10px;">The 13-mile Olentangy Trail between <a href="https://www.columbus.gov/recreationandparks/parks/Clinton-Como-Park/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" style="color: #003087; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;">Clinton-Como Park</a> and <a href="https://www.columbus.gov/recreationandparks/parks/Northmoor-Park/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: #003087; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;">Northmoor Park</a> is nearly complete! In response to feedback from the public, <a href="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/OHCCC/2023/03/01/file_attachments/2423676/North%20Broadway%20Crossing%20Safety%20Enhancement%20Summary.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: #003087; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;">several safety features</a> will be added to the crossing at North Broadway near OhioHealth and State Route 315.</p>
<h2 style="line-height: 1.1; font-weight: bold; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #CB343C; font-size: 18px; text-align: left; margin: 0 0 10px;" align="left">Safety enhancements include:</h2>
<ul>
<li style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 7px;">High visibility, oversized “No Turn On Red” LED signs that are activated when trail users press the pedestrian crossing button</li>
<li style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 7px;">A Leading Pedestrian Interval (LPI) was added to the signal timing, which gives trail users a three to seven second head start when entering the crosswalk, occurring before the corresponding green light signal activates for motorists</li>
<li style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 7px;">A raised concrete median so trail users will be easier for motorists to see in the crosswalk</li>
<li style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 7px;">Reboundable plastic pylons on the raised concrete median to identify the crossing as a high pedestrian area</li>
<li style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 7px;">Enhanced signage including yellow “Trail Crossing” signs</li>
<li style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 7px;">Plaza “queueing areas” on the north and south side of North Broadway to provide adequate space for trail users waiting for the crossing signal</li>
</ul>
<h2 style="line-height: 1.1; font-weight: bold; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #CB343C; font-size: 18px; text-align: left; margin: 0 0 10px;" align="left"> </h2>
<h2 style="line-height: 1.1; font-weight: bold; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #CB343C; font-size: 18px; text-align: left; margin: 0 0 10px;" align="left">Project Timeline</h2>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 10px;">Construction on this project is expected to begin in February 2024, and it is anticipated to be completed in February 2025. There will be no detours for this project. Trail users can continue using the current part of the Olentangy Trail. <a href="https://www.columbus.gov/recreationandparks/trails/Olentangy-Trail/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: #003087; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;">See the updated design with these additional safety features, and learn more about the Olentangy Trail project</a>.</p>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 10px;"> </p>
<h2 style="line-height: 1.1; font-weight: bold; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #CB343C; font-size: 18px; text-align: left; margin: 0 0 10px;" align="left">Project in the News</h2>
<ul>
<li style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 7px;">
<strong>Columbus Dispatch - </strong><a href="https://www.dispatch.com/story/news/local/2023/02/25/olentangy-trail-bicyclists-to-have-more-time-to-cross-new-intersection/69922955007/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: #003087; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;">Columbus plans more safety improvements at new Olentangy Trail crossing</a>
</li>
<li style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 7px;">
<strong>Columbus Underground - </strong><a href="https://columbusunderground.com/plan-to-close-clintonville-gap-in-olentangy-trail-moving-forward-bw1/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: #003087; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;">Plan to Close Clintonville Gap in Olentangy Trail Moving</a><a href="https://columbusunderground.com/plan-to-close-clintonville-gap-in-olentangy-trail-moving-forward-bw1/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: #003087; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;"> Forward</a>
</li>
<li style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 7px;">
<strong>NBC4</strong> - <a href="https://www.nbc4i.com/news/local-news/columbus/safety-improvements-coming-to-the-olentangy-trail/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: #003087; text-decoration: underline; -ms-word-break: break-all; word-break: break-word; -webkit-hyphens: none; -moz-hyphens: none; hyphens: none;">Safety improvements coming to the Olentangy Trail</a>
</li>
</ul>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #444446; margin: 0 0 10px;"> </p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</td>
</tr>

</table>
</td>
</tr>

</table></td></tr></table>]]>
